    "caption": "Cartier's movie necklace was mostly zirconia. In Ocean's 8, the target is a Cartier necklace called the Toussaint, named for Jeanne Toussaint, Cartier's creative director. The design came from a necklace made in 1931, and that original no longer exists. So Cartier rebuilt it in Paris from archive sketches. The copy is 15 to 20 percent smaller, to fit its wearer. Its stones are mostly zirconia, set in white gold. It was the only piece Cartier made just for the film. The rebuild took eight weeks.",
